/* SFGAO_CANLINK
 * row: SFGAO_CANLINK (0x00000004) Shortcuts can be created for the specified file objects or folders. This flag has the same value as DROPEFFECT. The typical use of this flag is to add a Create Shortcut item to the shortcut menu that is displayed during drag-and-drop operations. However, SFGAO_CANLINK also adds a Create Shortcut item to the Windows Explorer File menu, and to typical shortcut menus. If this item is selected, your application's IContextMenu::InvokeCommand interface is invoked with the lpVerb member of the CMINVOKECOMMANDINFO structure set to "link". Your application is responsible for creating the link.
